# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check these out
# with CRLF endings. bash then rejects the `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` shebang, and
# a pre-commit hook that cannot start aborts every commit.
#
# Deliberately narrow: a blanket `* text=auto` would also rewrite the golden
# outputs under tests/expected/, which are compared byte-for-byte against
# LF-emitting formatter output.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
